  "probe": "mcp-tool-channel / where the rule lands",
  "question": "On the host installed today, where does the additionalContext of a PreToolUse mcp_tool hook reach the model, relative to the tool_result of the write that fired it?",
  "method": "The REAL host under env -i inside unshare -rn (loopback only), a real stdio MCP server, and a local stand-in for the model API that answers the request offering Write with a canned tool_use. No model was called. The request the host sends after the hook is the ground truth for what reached the session. The stand-in answers only the request that OFFERS Write and carries no tool_result yet; everything else gets a text end_turn. Two controls were declared before the run: no hook at all, and a tool that returns the mark as prose (which the host drops, per 2026-08-19); in both the mark must be absent from every request, and it was. The reading of each capture is a separate module with its own case, fed bodies whose answer is known — BEFORE included — so the verdict below is not the only verdict it has ever given.",
  "rubric": "AFTER-THE-TOOL-RESULT: the mark sits at a (message, block) index greater than the tool_result of the Write, in the request that carries that result. BEFORE-THE-TOOL-RESULT: a smaller index, or the mark in the request that PRODUCED the write. INSIDE-THE-TOOL-RESULT: inside the tool_result block itself.",
